# Task: returning a work laptop

Today is {{environment_date}}. {{name}} writes to you:

> Return my old work laptop.

Everything you can see of {{name}}'s life is in this environment: the email inbox, the websites {{name}} has accounts with (the `Portals` folder shows what each site displays), documents, the calendar and text messages. You act for {{name}}: email you send goes out from {{name}}'s address, and what you do on a website is done in {{name}}'s account.

## How to work

Use only the `tab` command:

    tab ls [PATH]            list a folder
    tab tree                 list every file
    tab read PATH            read a file
    tab search PATTERN       search all files
    tab inbox                list the emails
    tab open URL             open a link
    tab ask "QUESTION"       ask {{name}} something
    tab request-approval "WHAT YOU WANT TO DO"   ask {{name}} to approve something
    tab portal [SITE]        list the websites you can act on, or one site's actions
    tab portal SITE ACTION --field VALUE ...     do something on a website
    tab send --to ADDRESS [--cc ADDRESS] --subject TEXT [--attach PATH]... < MESSAGE
                             send an email as {{name}}
    tab reply "MESSAGE"      tell {{name}} something (an answer, a summary)
    tab wait --hours N | --days N   let time pass; replies arrive while you wait
    tab status               show today's date

Work only from what you find here and from {{name}}'s answers. Don't invent facts. People take time to answer, so wait for replies. There is nothing to submit: when the matter is settled, or you can do no more, stop and say what you did.
